(7714415, 1268103, 123833, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> I know it''s supposed to be dark, yet it seems too light for me. It''s a beautiful photo. I''m curious if it''s the blue tones that are bothering me. It''s so blue on the snow. What happen''s if you tone down the blue or warm up the image? </i></td></tr></table> I read somewhere that Tungsten WB is good for the night sky so that''s probably were the colors came from ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: I know it''s supposed to be dark, yet it seems too light for me. It''s a beautiful photo. I''m curious if it''s the blue tones that are bothering me. It''s so blue on the snow. What happen''s if you tone down the blue or warm up the image?  I read somewhere that Tungsten WB is good for the night sky so that''s probably were the colors came from ;)', '2022-02-14 02:02:41.000000', NULL, 0),
